author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: Adapt pm-jev tooling; no scheduled release; full authored source coverage; documentation and duplication clean; npm and Bun release gates; npm/npx and native Bun/bunx packed installs; real public read-only acceptance.
parent: pm-review-epic
release: 2026.10.12
resolution: Implemented and merged in #1 (fcf34e5).
expected_result: The change described by this item is on main.
actual_result: "Merged in #1 as fcf34e5; checks successful at head 3161974: CodeQL, codeql, test (22), test (26)."
comments[21]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-12T10:55:51.852Z",pi-glm-quality,"Plan: implement scripts/main-invocation.ts, scripts/docstring-gate.ts and a compact c8-based scripts/coverage-gate.ts (package.json coverageGate config; c8 --all include src+scripts+root entry, exclude tests/dist/node_modules; json-summary/json/lcov; report invalidation on start and failure; disk-inventory reconciliation against the summary). Cover scripts via test/tooling.test.ts (real child executions plus importable functions; c8 aggregates child coverage) and add test/install.acceptance.ts (pack allowlist, isolated npm+Bun consumers, real SDK temp trackers, npx/bunx registration). Review .github workflows against the scaffolded package; expected no-op since guards already reference PM_REVIEW_RELEASE_ENABLED and workflow_dispatch only."
  "2026-10-12T11:16:46.204Z",codex-sol,"Orchestrator adopted and verified the CLI worker drafts after the GLM quota check showed only four percent remaining. Further worker calls were stopped. Packed npm/npx and native Bun/bunx consumers both passed: allowlisted tarball, four command help surfaces, typed schema registration, offline precedent query and search in independent real trackers. Coverage and full release gates are still being completed."
  "2026-10-12T11:37:35.004Z",codex-sol,"Final quality receipts: fresh npm ci passed; both full npm and Bun gates and the isolated Git-identity full npm gate passed. Packed artifacts passed in independent npm/npx and native Bun/bunx workspaces. The fixture-backed transport and real tracker tests pass at unchanged 100/100/100/100 thresholds. Four development audit entries from one braces advisory remain tracked by pm-review-dev-audit; production audit is clean."
  "2026-10-12T11:50:22.757Z",codex-sol,"Final acceptance hygiene correction: npm pack now receives a scratch HOME rather than the package directory, keeping package-manager logs and cache in the disposable consumer fixture. Runtime code and the packed allowlist are unchanged. Package-local caches remain ignored."
  "2026-10-12T12:31:48.639Z",codex-sol,"Final full-gate verification is complete at source commit 5fe85ac under npm, Bun and isolated Git identity. npm pack --dry-run lists 37 allowlisted files; packed consumer acceptance passes npm/npx and native Bun/bunx. SDK type-registration and normal-home global-extension version skew remain tracked by pm-review-sdk-gap; the four development audit entries from one underlying braces advisory remain tracked by pm-review-dev-audit. Release workflow remains dispatch-only and maintainer-disabled. Claims are released for orchestrator review; no items are closed."
  "2026-10-12T13:22:57.223Z",codex-sol,"Review round 1 confirms missing identity enforcement, broken release epic link, ignored eval queries, and root-source coverage glob. Add minimal behavioral regressions and independently revert each fix before recording proof."
  "2026-10-12T13:30:18.594Z",codex-sol,"Finding 4248463199: added identity-gate.ts to required CI and release checks. Real Git regression rejects unapproved author/committer identities, private home paths and side-branch history. Behavioral revert of auditIdentities to no enforcement fails identity policy rejects unapproved (exit 1); reverting only CI wiring fails identity policy runs as a required (exit 1)."
  "2026-10-12T13:30:19.861Z",codex-sol,"Finding 4248463231: release PR body now links the existing pm-review-epic. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"release PR tracking link\" test/tooling.test.ts passes; reverting only that link fails the same test (exit 1, missing tracked epic)."
  "2026-10-12T13:30:21.115Z",codex-sol,"Finding 4248463257: removed parent search-directory ignore. Real Git check-ignore now includes eval-queries.json while excluding generated search files. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"Git includes eval queries\" test/tooling.test.ts passes; reverting only the ignore fix fails (exit 1)."
  "2026-10-12T13:30:22.626Z",codex-sol,"Finding 4248463262: root sources normalize to . and use **/*.ts. Real c8 fixture at 100/100/100/100 passes with sources=[.]. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"coverage gate measures repository-root\" test/tooling.test.ts passes; reverting only inventorySources fails (exit 1, source absent from report)."
  "2026-10-12T13:32:35.571Z",codex-sol,"Round 1 preliminary full coverage passes 82/82 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips/todos, with 100/100/100/100 over all 17 configured authored source files. All eleven findings have targeted isolated revert proofs; identity enforcement also has a separate CI-wiring proof. Final committed-head npm, Bun, isolated-identity and Node 22 release checks follow."
  "2026-10-12T13:41:48.517Z",codex-sol,"Node 22 full release check uncovered a second acceptance fixture defect after the timeout fix: npm 10 runs prepare during npm pack --ignore-scripts, while source-package packing supplied an uninitialized consumer PM_PATH. Use the source package tracker for source packing; consumer install and command trackers remain isolated. The existing real packed npm/Bun acceptance is the regression."
  "2026-10-12T13:44:48.222Z",codex-sol,"Additional Node 22 acceptance correction: source packing uses the source PM tracker and parses the final npm JSON array after npm 10 prepare output. npm run test:install under Node 22.23.1/npm 10.9.8 passes 1/1 with both npm/npx and native Bun/bunx consumers. Reverting only the tracker coordinate fails with Tracker is not initialized (exit 1); reverting only JSON-prefix handling fails with SyntaxError (exit 1). No consumer scenario or lifecycle check was skipped."
  "2026-10-13T12:43:11.254Z",codex-agent,"Review round two takeover: inspect existing uncommitted tooling fixes, independently run one-change revert proofs, then full npm and Bun release gates. Preserve historical records and commit only explicit package-owned paths."
  "2026-10-13T12:48:48.588Z",codex-agent,"Independently verified tooling revert proofs: pack manifest parser, coverage root anchoring, and identity patch buffer each fail their focused behavioral regression with the one file reverted to HEAD (exit 1), then pass after byte-for-byte restoration (exit 0). Added an actual relative-root coverage CLI invocation alongside the deterministic runner regression."
  "2026-10-13T12:52:07.837Z",codex-agent,First linked npm release check correctly failed on require-atomic-updates in the added CLI-error regression. Replaced mutable shared test contexts with fresh contexts; no production change was needed. Rerunning the complete gate. Remaining dogfood UX is tracked by pm-review-summary-ux (static-analysis wrapper title) and pm-review-help-ux (host help placeholders).
  "2026-10-13T12:56:12.309Z",codex-agent,"The zero-duplication gate caught repeated test setup after the first lint correction. Consolidated the new expected-error assertions into the existing validation/network-boundary test, retaining its previous checks. Lint and duplication now pass at the unchanged zero threshold. The linked standalone core run reached its default 120-second timeout under concurrent host load; full release gates have a 2400-second budget and are still running."
  "2026-10-13T13:01:33.486Z",codex-agent,"Full npm gate reached changelog validation: all 85 coverage tests passed with no skips at 100 statements, branches, functions and lines across 17 authored sources; production audit reports zero vulnerabilities. Changelog entry ordering changed after PM mutations, so regenerating the checked changelog and rerunning both full gates. The five one-change revert proofs remain independently verified."
  "2026-10-13T13:27:25.767Z",codex-agent,"Final certification passed: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each exit 0 through linked PM test runs. Both cover 85 passing tests, no skips, 100 statements/branches/functions/lines over 17 authored sources, zero duplication, clean production audit, changelog, publish attestation and real packed npm/npx plus native Bun/bunx consumers. All five restored production hashes match. Evidence is in docs/review-round2.md; original scratch task/rules files remain unavailable. Remaining UX is tracked by pm-review-summary-ux and pm-review-help-ux."
  "2026-10-13T18:38:12.740Z",claude-hub,"CodeRabbit round 3 (identity gate, Major): the home-path pattern matched relative names such as a root-named source file or a root-cause document, because the root-home alternative only required a word boundary; any false positive fails every later gate run while the commit stays in the audited range. Extracted containsAbsoluteHomePath() anchored to path boundaries. Table test 'home-path detection is anchored to path boundaries' (10 detected, 7 ignored; fixtures built from string parts so the test itself adds no literal paths). Revert proof: restoring the old pattern fails on the root-named source file case."
  "2026-10-13T21:40:33.497Z",claude-hub,"CodeRabbit round 6 (release.yml merge loop, security): auto-resolution of release-PR review threads now requires every comment author to be an allowlisted review bot (coderabbitai), so code-scanning and other app findings are never silently resolved; each resolution is written to the step summary. Test 'release PR auto-resolution only touches threads written entirely by the allowlisted review bot' runs the workflow's own jq filter against review-bot, code-scanning, mixed-bot and human threads; removing the allowlist fails it. CHANGELOG regenerated with changelog:full (the check uses replace mode; prepend mode caused the previous CI failure)."
